<%# The summary a form shows when it comes back. Two things earn their keep here
    beyond listing the messages:

    - Each message is a **link to the field it is about**. `form.text_field :name`
      renders id="user_name", which is what `field_id` rebuilds, and navigating
      to a fragment focuses the target when it is focusable — so a student fixes
      the problem by clicking it rather than by re-reading the form. An error on
      :base (the terms checkbox) belongs to no field and stays plain text.
    - `tabindex="-1"` makes the panel itself focusable, so those links have
      somewhere to send a keyboard user back to. `role=alert` is what announces
      the panel when it appears.

    The heading counts nothing — the list is what says how many and which — so
    auth.errors_title takes no interpolation and needs no plural forms. %>
<% if record.errors.any? %>
  <div role="alert" tabindex="-1"
       class="mb-5 rounded-field border border-danger-line border-l-[3px] border-l-brand-alert bg-danger-tint
              px-4 py-3.5 text-14 leading-[1.55] text-brand-accent">
    <p class="flex items-center gap-2.5 font-bold">
      <span aria-hidden="true"
            class="grid size-5 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-alert text-12 font-bold text-white">!</span>
      <%= t("auth.errors_title") %>
    </p>

    <ul class="mt-2 flex list-disc flex-col gap-1.5 pl-11 marker:text-brand-alert">
      <% record.errors.each do |error| %>
        <li>
          <% if error.attribute == :base %>
            <%= error.full_message %>
          <% else %>
            <%= link_to error.full_message, "##{field_id(record, error.attribute)}",
                  class: "underline decoration-brand-alert underline-offset-[3px]
                          transition-colors hover:text-brand-deep hover:decoration-brand-deep" %>
          <% end %>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  </div>
<% end %>
